Hotel Management System

// Functional Requirements (FR)

User should be able to search hotels by location.
User should be able to view hotel details.
User should be able to view available rooms.
User should be able to book a room.
System should generate a Booking ID.
User should be able to make payment.
System should confirm booking after successful payment.
System should mark the room as occupied/booked.
User should be able to cancel a booking.
System should release the room after cancellation.
User should be able to check-in using the Booking ID.
User should be able to check-out.
System should calculate the total bill based on the stay duration.


// Non Functional Requirements (NFR)

Design should be modular.
Design should follow SOLID principles.
Low coupling and high cohesion.
Design should be scalable.
Design should be maintainable and testable.
Design should support multiple payment methods.
Design should support multiple room types in the future.


